# Files that are read by Linux, whoever checks them out.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for this repo, so a checkout on Windows converts LF to
# CRLF. That is right for source, and wrong for anything a container executes:
# `#!/bin/bash\r` fails with "no such file or directory", naming a file that is
# plainly there. Same for the SQL and entrypoints these mount.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker/* text eol=lf
supabase/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
